# SABOTAGE: the PER-SURFACE unread branches added by the fail-honest sweep are dropped — the
# activity feed, deliverability and flag-admin render sites lose their `unread` gate, and the three
# read layers behind them collapse their marker back to a constant `nil`.
#
# This is aimed at the ADOPTION, outside the primitive: `Samen.UI.unread_state/1`, `%Page.unread`
# and `list_view/1`'s clause are all untouched (patch 338 owns those, and the page still KNOWS when
# a read failed — it simply has no per-surface statement to make). What is lost is the
# disambiguation each of these three surfaces gained: an empty feed reads as "No changes in this
# window.", an unreadable suppression list reads as "No suppressions.", an unreadable cohort read
# reads as "No tenant accounts yet." — each an assertion about data the surface never observed.
#
# No warning is introduced (the read-layer functions that reported `ok?` are still called, their
# results simply discarded, and `unread_deliverability/0` is removed with its only call site), and
# the replay runs `mix test`, so there is no warning to confine.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/unread_is_not_empty_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: the deliverability read layer marks a FAILED read, and never a successful one
# MUST_FAIL: the deliverability page names the unread silence for both tables, and the readable one for neither
# MUST_FAIL: the flags cohort read reports which silence it is, and the page renders it
# MUST_FAIL: the activity feed separates an UNREADABLE tier from an empty window
